---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = '30 June 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="TransferHub privacy policy — how we collect, use, share and protect your data, including cookies, Google AdSense, analytics, and your GDPR/CCPA rights."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl prose prose-gray prose-headings:text-gray-900 prose-p:text-gray-600 prose-li:text-gray-600 prose-a:text-emerald-600 prose-h1:font-black prose-h2:font-bold prose-h2:text-lg">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-cream-dim text-sm not-prose">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>TransferHub ("we", "us", "our") operates the website at transferhub.club (the "Site"). This policy explains what data we process, why, the legal bases we rely on, who we share it with, and the rights you have. By using the Site you agree to this policy.</p>

    <h2>1. Who is the data controller</h2>
    <p>TransferHub is the controller for personal data processed through the Site. For any privacy request, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@transferhub.net">privacy@transferhub.net</a>.</p>

    <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Usage &amp; device data</strong> — pages viewed, referring URL, approximate location (country/region), browser type, device type, and interaction events, collected via analytics cookies.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising identifiers &amp; cookies</strong> — set by Google AdSense and its partners to serve and measure ads (see Section 5).</li>
      <li><strong>Consent records</strong> — your cookie-consent choice and timestamp, stored locally in your browser.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> ask for or store names, emails, passwords, or payment data. We do not run user accounts.</p>

    <h2>3. Why we process it (legal bases)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Consent</strong> (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)) — for non-essential analytics and personalized advertising cookies. You may withdraw consent at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)) — for basic, aggregated, non-identifying measurement to keep the Site running and secure.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>We use: <strong>strictly necessary</strong> cookies (always on, needed for the Site to function); <strong>analytics</strong> cookies (Google Analytics, only with consent); and <strong>advertising</strong> cookies (Google AdSense and partners, only with consent). You can change or withdraw your choice anytime via the "Cookie settings" link in the footer, or by clearing cookies in your browser.</p>

    <h2>5. Advertising — Google AdSense &amp; partners</h2>
    <p>We display ads through Google AdSense. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits. You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
      <li>For users in the EEA/UK, we use a consent mechanism compliant with Google's EU User Consent Policy; ads are non-personalized unless you consent.</li>
      <li>You can review third-party vendors and opt-outs at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a> and <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</li>
      <li>Google's own privacy practices: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Analytics</h2>
    <p>We use Google Analytics (with IP anonymization where available) to understand aggregate traffic. Analytics runs only after you consent. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>7. Sharing &amp; international transfers</h2>
    <p>We share data only with the service providers above (Google for ads/analytics, and our hosting provider Vercel) strictly to operate the Site. These providers may process data outside your country, including the United States, under appropriate safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>

    <h2>8. Data retention</h2>
    <p>Analytics and advertising data are retained per the providers' standard periods. Your local consent record persists until you clear it or it expires after 12 months.</p>

    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p><strong>EEA/UK (GDPR):</strong> access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection, portability, and the right to withdraw consent and to lodge a complaint with your supervisory authority.</p>
    <p><strong>California (CCPA/CPRA):</strong> the right to know, delete, and opt out of "sale"/"sharing" of personal information. We do not sell personal information for money; some ad cookies may constitute "sharing" under CPRA — use "Cookie settings" to opt out.</p>
    <p>To exercise any right, email <a href="mailto:privacy@transferhub.net">privacy@transferhub.net</a>.</p>

    <h2>10. Children</h2>
    <p>The Site is not directed to children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect their data. If you believe a child has provided data, contact us for removal.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy; material changes will be reflected by the "Last updated" date above.</p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@transferhub.net">privacy@transferhub.net</a> or our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
